Z||000000||85fierogt||08-06-2001||12:06 AM||||anyway when i pores sthe switch to pop my trunk on the dash the little brake light on the dash comes on.........dont know how do i fix it?<BR>thanxs<BR>P.S i just bought this car and its my first fiero so thats why im full of questions<BR>-brad||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||08-06-2001||12:50 AM||||They do that.  That's just the way the circuit was designed.  It has to do with the fact that they didn't want somebody to pop open the trunk lid while the car was in motion.  So, the only time the electric trunk release will operate is 1)when the ignition is switched off, or 2)if ignition is on, and the parking brake is applied.  Try it and see for yourself.<P>It is possible to keep the "brake" light in the dash from coming on when you operate the electric trunk release, by wiring in a diode.  But it doesn't hurt anything, really, does it?  So the next time you pop the trunk and see the "brake" light come on, just say to yourself, "Them's the brakes!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||08-06-2001||01:53 AM||||It also matters if its a stick or an auto. But as for the brake light coming on I have never heard of that one.||||reg||1
