Z||000008||StuGood||08-07-2001||09:23 AM||||All right, here's the scoop on the circuit.  Look at <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/screwup.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/screwup.html</A>  scroll down to "The curious brake warning light explanation," and have a read.<P>As far as diagnosing the trunk popper no-workee, you might try unplugging the solenoid at the trunk latch.  Probe the solenoid with a fused jumper from a 12v source, and see if the solenoid works. If solenoid works, plug a meter or test light into the wire you just disconnected - you should get 12v when someone operates the trunk release button, <B>if</B> the ignition is off.   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jncomutt||08-07-2001||09:51 AM||||On my 84, the trunk will open whenever you press the switch.  Even opens while driving around.  It will not work if the car is off however.  Also, the hand brake seems to have no effect on when it works.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Carrolles||08-08-2001||08:05 AM||||The trunk release solenoid is grounded through the trunk latch when the trunk is closed.  If it is open and you probe the solenoid wire with a 12+ source nothing will happen.  Connect a jumper cable between the solenoid frame and a good ground then try.||||reg||1
